<title>SWITZERLAND: Esec sees 1997/98 sales up to 480 mln Sfr.</title>
<headline>Esec sees 1997/98 sales up to 480 mln Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss microchip equipment manufacturer Esec Holding said it expected group sales to rise to 480 million Swiss francs in the year ending on February 28, 1998 from 345 million in the past year.</p>
<p>The company said in its annual report it expected a return on sales of more than 10 percent.</p>
<p>It saw sales over one billion francs in the year 2000.</p>
<p>Esec's 1996/97 group net dropped to 11 million from 26 million after it took special charges of eight million. It cut its dividend to 4.20 francs per share from 11.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
